<title>INDIA: India's SRF to offer rights issue.</title>
<headline>India's SRF to offer rights issue.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian tyre cord maker SRF Ltd said on Tuesday that it planned to offer a rights issue which would raise some 205 million rupees in fresh equity.</p>
<p>Vice-chairman Arun Bharat Ram told a news conference in the Indian capital that SRF forecast 1996/97 (April-March) sales at about six billion rupees, up from 4.9 billion in the previous fiscal year.  </p>
<p>SRF officials said the rights issue would be offered in four to five months.</p>
<p>Earlier on Tuesday, SRF said GE Capital Services, a unit of U.S.-based General Electric Co, would pay 53.50 rupees per share for its 50.5 percent stake in SRF Finance Ltd.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
